Description: 
  Provides a collection of routines for evaluating data from
  larger forest management units, typically sample inventories, but also 
  stand-wise inventories. The idea is to support modern forest planning
  approaches and to be open by design to new data sources and evaluation
  methods. For the methodological background of forest inventories see
  Kangas and Maltamo (2006) "Forest Inventory: Methodology and Applications"
  <doi:10.1007/1-4020-4381-3>.
